# Downloading ACS Tables
Here are **good practice/steps** on how to download the data from the [US Census Website](https://data.census.gov/).

## 1-Look-Up ACS Table
Start by looking up the specific ACS Table (using table ID)
- For example: ``C17002``
## 2-Select ACS Tables Product
After looking up and selection the ACS Table, make sure to select the desired product.
- For example:
    1) ``2025: ACS 1-Year Estimates Detailed Tables``
    2) ``2024: ACS 5-Year Estimates Detailed Tables``   

    <div align="center">
    <img src="screenshots\Select-ACS-Tables-Product.png" alt="UI Screenshot of selecting a ACS Product." width="600" height="300">
    </div>

## 3-Setting Geography Filter
When downloading ACS Data, you should set a geography filter. For the MPOs purposes, there are two common filters that are used in the core documents and interactive products:
1) Mapping Geography Filter
2) Tabuler Geography Filter

---

### **Mapping Geography Filter**
The Map data filter is used when downloading data for the GIS Systems and mainly the Demographic Profile App. What makes this filter different is the geography level of the data and GEOID column connections for the GIS System use. The geographic filter will be on the ``Census Track, Block Group, Block`` level with both ``Jackson and Josephine Counties`` as geographic boundary of the data.   
- For Mapping purposes, the geographic filter will be on the ``Census Track, Block Group, Block`` level including both ``Jackson and Josephine Counties``.
    
